      "explanation": "1.6.1 learns the BPE codes once on every drug of the dataset (`create_pharmaformer_drug_embeddings`, a script run before any split), so a drug that is only tested is encoded with codes that saw its SMILES. v2 learns them in the drug featurizer from the drugs of the training fold only (documented in `docs/explanation/literature_models.rst`), so the same SMILES is encoded differently and every number downstream differs.",
