  "findings": [
    "The network is the 1.6.1 network apart from docstrings, so a `state_dict` loads into both with `strict=True` and the forward pass agrees at the `forward` class in eval and in train mode.",
    "The v2 preset (commit 174ceea7, B5) is `pharmaFormerGeneExpression` with `gene_list: landmark_genes`, the 867-gene list of 1.6.1 (`PharmaFormerModel.gene_list`). The case does not override it; the selected columns agree (`*/features_sample`). The v2 featurizer fits both scalers on the unique training samples (`fit_on_unique_ids`), as 1.6.1 fits them on `np.unique(output.cell_line_ids)`.",
    "The training loop is the 1.6.1 loop: Adam without weight decay, MSE on `outputs.squeeze()`, the best validation epoch checkpointed and reloaded, early stop when the epochs without improvement reach `patience`. Both sides draw the shuffling permutation after the module initialization and a DataLoader base seed, so the torch RNG order is identical and the seeded runs agree at the `train` class.",
    "Both versions use one `dropout` value for the encoder layers and the head and no extra dropout (the documented omission concerns the published fine-tuning variant, which neither 1.6.1 nor v2 implements).",
    "The BPE codes are learned on every drug in 1.6.1 and on the training drugs in v2; with all drugs in training the codes and the encoded rows are identical (`*/bpe`), with a drug held out of training its test row and the predictions on it differ (deviation `unseen_drug/bpe_test` and `unseen_drug/predictions`; the rows of the training drugs and the trained parameters still agree in this case because the held-out drug does not change their merges).",
    "Both predictors require early-stopping data; v2 raises `ValueError` without it like 1.6.1.",
    "1.6.1 crashes when the last batch of an epoch (training or early-stopping) holds a single pair: `outputs.squeeze()` is 0-d and `np.concatenate` of the collected predictions raises `ValueError` (measured with 17 early-stopping pairs and batch size 8). v2 trains the same expression through `run_epoch`, which collects no predictions and so does not crash, but the 0-d against `(1,)` MSE broadcasts with a `UserWarning` as in 1.6.1. The case keeps every batch larger than one pair."
  ],
